# Every production `?` on a band reading inside a rung's reader (a
# closure passed to one of the ladder's entry points, `pub fn climb*` in
# `geom_core::ladder`; a `let` closure it reads through; or the closure a
# direct caller passes for a parameter it reads), counted per `fn` the
# reader is written in
# (scripts/gates/escalation-question-marks.sh, `escalation_rungs.py`).
# A new site reds until it is registered here with why its `?` is not a
# search inside the rung; a count that falls reds until it is lowered.
#
# Two dispositions, named per entry:
# - PREMISE: each read a `?` stops is read only on what the reads before
#   it placed, so the first refusal is the rung's own, not a kept
#   reading a later read of the same rung answers past.
# - SEARCH: a later read is independent of the earlier and could answer
#   for the rung alone: read both before either refuses (the port), and
#   lower the count. Each is listed with its port in
#   work/onecopy/a-rungs-later-read-answers-past-its-earlier-question-mark.md.
#
# held_cut's cut: `nested` (a strut's) answers `false`, as `on_arc`'s
# `Some(false)` does on its own: SEARCH. `on_arc`, then `tied_held` only
# on the end `on_arc` tied: PREMISE.
rung:crates/topo/src/boolean/insert.rs:held_cut 4
# FaceOnLocus::at's ride (climb_differing): the end (`hi - s`) is read
# only where the start decided inside, and is the rung's last read; the
# start's own refusal is an `and_then`, not a `?`: PREMISE.
rung:crates/topo/src/boolean/rim_wedge.rs:at 1
# crescent's pair of bounds. The opening (`bool_sector_crescent`) reads
# none of the reads before it, and decided off `Positive` it answers
# `false` alone. So the first `parallel_same_as`, the across reading and
# `coincident_run` each refuse ahead of it: SEARCH (the first
# `parallel_same_as` also ahead of the across reading). The second
# `parallel_same_as`, read only under `coincident_run`: PREMISE.
rung:crates/topo/src/boolean/sectors.rs:crescent 5
# path_parity's piece against an arc: `plane_roots` refuses ahead of
# `misses_in_plane`, whose coplanar-apart arm holds whatever the planes:
# SEARCH. The meridian arm's `plane_roots`, `segment_misses` and the
# lead's length on an end already decided on the plane, and
# `spline_crossings` alone in its arm: PREMISE. Both arms that read a
# segment's two ends read them together, since an end decided on the
# cylinder or the plane answers alone.
rung:crates/topo/src/ring_path.rs:path_parity 6
# ruled_region's apex walk, a reader `ray_walk::walk` reads through its
# parameter: `apex_generator` builds the generator `read_leg` reads:
# PREMISE.
rung:crates/topo/src/boolean/ruled_region.rs:contains 1
# point_in_faces' ray sweep, read the same way: `missed_side` is read
# only where `cast_ray` found no hit: PREMISE.
rung:crates/topo/src/boolean/solid_contain.rs:point_in_faces 1
